! DBG89.DBG - SET SCOPE on a recursion (README.md), stopped in LEAF under
! REC(1), REC(2), REC(3), and START. VMS's log leaves out a command that
! fails, so a comment names each case first.
SHOW MODULE
SET BREAK INLEAF
GO
SHOW CALLS
!> SHOW SCOPE, the default
SHOW SCOPE
!> Scope 0's registers
EXAMINE R0
EXAMINE R1
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE R5
EXAMINE R6
EXAMINE R7
EXAMINE AP
EXAMINE FP
EXAMINE SP
EXAMINE PC
EXAMINE PSL
!> EXAMINE Y, from LEAF
EXAMINE Y
!> EXAMINE Z, only in the module not set
EXAMINE Z
!> Numeric path names: EXAMINE 0\Y
EXAMINE 0\Y
!> EXAMINE 1\R2
EXAMINE 1\R2
!> EXAMINE 1\%R2
EXAMINE 1\%R2
!> EXAMINE 2\%R2
EXAMINE 2\%R2
!> EXAMINE 4\%R2
EXAMINE 4\%R2
!> EXAMINE 9\%R2, past the stack
EXAMINE 9\%R2
!> EXAMINE 1\%PC
EXAMINE 1\%PC
!> EXAMINE 1\%FP
EXAMINE 1\%FP
!> Invocation numbers: EXAMINE REC 0\%R2
EXAMINE REC 0\%R2
!> EXAMINE REC 1\%R2
EXAMINE REC 1\%R2
!> EXAMINE DBG89\REC 2\%R2
EXAMINE DBG89\REC 2\%R2
!> EXAMINE REC 3\%R2, one more than there are
EXAMINE REC 3\%R2
!> EXAMINE REC\%R2
EXAMINE REC\%R2
!> EXAMINE START\%R2
EXAMINE START\%R2
!> EXAMINE DBG89B\%R2, a routine not active
EXAMINE DBG89B\%R2
!> EXAMINE REC 1\Y
EXAMINE REC 1\Y
!> EXAMINE/INSTRUCTION REC 1\%PC
EXAMINE/INSTRUCTION REC 1\%PC
!> The built-in scope symbols
EVALUATE %CURRENT_SCOPE_ENTRY
EVALUATE %NEXT_SCOPE_ENTRY
!> EVALUATE %PREVIOUS_SCOPE_ENTRY at scope 0
EVALUATE %PREVIOUS_SCOPE_ENTRY
!> SET SCOPE 1
SET SCOPE 1
SHOW SCOPE
SHOW CALLS
EXAMINE R0
EXAMINE R1
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE R3
EXAMINE R5
EXAMINE R6
EXAMINE R7
EXAMINE AP
EXAMINE FP
EXAMINE SP
EXAMINE PC
EXAMINE PSL
!> EXAMINE .PC
EXAMINE .PC
!> EXAMINE/INSTRUCTION .PC
EXAMINE/INSTRUCTION .PC
!> EXAMINE .AP+4, REC(1)'s argument
EXAMINE .AP+4
!> EXAMINE .(.AP+4)
EXAMINE .(.AP+4)
!> EXAMINE Y
EXAMINE Y
!> EXAMINE with no address, after a register
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE
!> EVALUATE R2+1
EVALUATE R2+1
!> EVALUATE %CURRENT_SCOPE_ENTRY
EVALUATE %CURRENT_SCOPE_ENTRY
EVALUATE %NEXT_SCOPE_ENTRY
EVALUATE %PREVIOUS_SCOPE_ENTRY
!> EXAMINE 0\%R2 under SET SCOPE 1
EXAMINE 0\%R2
!> SET SCOPE 2
SET SCOPE 2
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE R3
EXAMINE R4
EXAMINE R5
EXAMINE R6
EXAMINE AP
EXAMINE FP
EXAMINE PC
!> SET SCOPE 4, START
SET SCOPE 4
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE R5
EXAMINE R6
EXAMINE PC
!> SET SCOPE 5, below START
SET SCOPE 5
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE PC
!> SET SCOPE 9, past the stack
SET SCOPE 9
SHOW SCOPE
!> EXAMINE R2 under SET SCOPE 9
EXAMINE R2
!> SET SCOPE 1, 0, a list
SET SCOPE 1, 0
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE R2
!> SET SCOPE \
SET SCOPE \
SHOW SCOPE
!> EXAMINE Y under SET SCOPE \
EXAMINE Y
!> EXAMINE R2 under SET SCOPE \
EXAMINE R2
!> SET SCOPE DBG89\REC, a routine with three activations
SET SCOPE DBG89\REC
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE PC
!> SET SCOPE REC 1
SET SCOPE REC 1
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE R2
!> SET SCOPE DBG89B, the routine of a module not set
SET SCOPE DBG89B
SHOW SCOPE
SHOW MODULE
!> EXAMINE Y under SET SCOPE DBG89B
EXAMINE Y
!> EXAMINE Z under SET SCOPE DBG89B
EXAMINE Z
!> EXAMINE R2 under SET SCOPE DBG89B
EXAMINE R2
!> SET SCOPE/MODULE DBG89B
SET SCOPE/MODULE DBG89B
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE Y
!> SET SCOPE/MODULE DBG89
SET SCOPE/MODULE DBG89
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE Y
!> SET SCOPE DBG89B, 1
SET SCOPE DBG89B, 1
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE Y
EXAMINE R2
!> SET SCOPE NOSUCH
SET SCOPE NOSUCH
SHOW SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1 while a SET SCOPE list is in effect
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1
SHOW SCOPE
!> CANCEL SCOPE
CANCEL SCOPE
SHOW SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1
SHOW SCOPE
SHOW CALLS
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE PC
EXAMINE Y
EVALUATE %CURRENT_SCOPE_ENTRY
EVALUATE %NEXT_SCOPE_ENTRY
EVALUATE %PREVIOUS_SCOPE_ENTRY
!> EXAMINE/SOURCE .PC under SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1
EXAMINE/SOURCE .PC
!> TYPE with no line, under SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1
TYPE
!> SET SCOPE/CURRENT 3 over /CURRENT 1
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 3
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE R2
!> SET SCOPE/CURRENT 0
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 0
SHOW SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE/CURRENT 9, past the stack
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 9
SHOW SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE/CURRENT REC, not a number
SET SCOPE/CURRENT REC
!> SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1, 2, a list
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1, 2
!> SET SCOPE/CURRENT with no parameter
SET SCOPE/CURRENT
!> SET SCOPE with no parameter
SET SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE %NEXT_SCOPE_ENTRY
CANCEL SCOPE
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1
SET SCOPE/CURRENT %NEXT_SCOPE_ENTRY
SHOW SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1, then STEP: is it kept?
CANCEL SCOPE
SET SCOPE/CURRENT 1
STEP/INSTRUCTION
SHOW SCOPE
!> SET SCOPE 1, then STEP: is it kept, and where does 1 point now?
SET SCOPE 1
SHOW SCOPE
STEP/INSTRUCTION
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE PC
CANCEL SCOPE
!> DEPOSIT to a register in scope 2 (REC(2)'s frame, now that LEAF has
!> returned): where does it go?
SET SCOPE 2
EXAMINE R2
DEPOSIT R2 = ^X2222
EXAMINE R2
!> DEPOSIT R5 in scope 2, which no frame saved
DEPOSIT R5 = ^X5555
EXAMINE R5
CANCEL SCOPE
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE R5
!> REC(1) returns to REC(2): R2 from its frame
SET BREAK BACK
GO
SHOW CALLS
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE R2
EXAMINE R5
!> SET SCOPE 1 at BACK, then GO: kept across GO? REC(2) returns to REC(3),
!> its R2 from the frame the DEPOSIT wrote
SET SCOPE 1
SHOW SCOPE
GO
SHOW CALLS
SHOW SCOPE
EXAMINE R2
CANCEL SCOPE
CANCEL BREAK/ALL
!> GO to the end
GO
